      "evidenceStatus": "TEACHING_APPROXIMATION_USER_EDITABLE",
      "provenance": "Teaching approximation, not a model of a real motor: ABB 3GAA112320-BDK (4 kW 4P IE3) data sheet 400 V D 50 Hz 8.60 A cos phi 0.770 eff 88.6 %, 1451 r/min, Is/In 7.6; IEC 60034-30-1:2014 IE3 4 kW 4P 50 Hz = 88.6 %.",
      "derivation": "Per winding section: Pin = ratedPowerKw / efficiency (or inputPowerKw), Psec = Pin / sections, |Z| = Vsec^2 * PF / Psec, R = |Z| * PF, X = |Z| * sin(acos PF) at referenceHz (X scales with f). DC winding R = statorLossShare * (Pin - Pout) / (sections * Isec^2).",
      "speedTorqueModel": "T-equivalent per section derived from this running point, the DC winding R, ratedMotorRpm, motorConfig.motorPoles and lockedRotorCurrentRatio (X1 = X2 assumed, IEEE 112). Slip follows supply voltage, frequency and motorLoadTorquePercent of the rated torque (default 100 = this running point); the stamped impedance follows slip, so the start draws the locked-rotor current.",
